      "nets": ["/CAN0_N", "/CAN0_P", "/CAN1_N", "/CAN1_P", "Net-(R34-Pad2)", "Net-(R35-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The two DIP-switch poles are wired across the CAN channels: SW6.1 and SW6.2 connect the far ends of the CAN0 and CAN1 termination resistors, while SW6.3 and SW6.4 connect CAN1_P and CAN0_P. Closing the latter pole directly joins the two positive bus lines; the termination resistors are not switched across their respective CAN pairs.",
      "expected": "CAN0 and CAN1 should remain independent, and any selectable termination should connect each 120R resistor across its own bus pair. The specification describes two separate isolated CAN buses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/CAN0_P\") ... (node (ref \"SW6\") (pin \"4\")) ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"7\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/CAN1_P\") ... (node (ref \"SW6\") (pin \"3\")) ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"7\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(R34-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"SW6\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(R35-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"SW6\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/CAN0_N\") ... (node (ref \"R34\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/CAN1_N\") ... (node (ref \"R35\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R34\") (value \"120R\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R35\") (value \"120R\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Switching on the pole between SW6.3 and SW6.4 shorts CAN0_P to CAN1_P. The other pole links the termination-resistor branches rather than providing proper independent bus termination, potentially disrupting both CAN buses.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R36 is assigned a schematic value of 24k, but its sourcing metadata identifies MPN FRC0805J240TSD and describes the part as 24Ω.",
      "expected": "The sourced part should match the intended 24k value, or the schematic value should be corrected if 24Ω is intended. A 24Ω part across VOUTN and VOUTP would not implement the specified 24k resistance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"VOUTN\") ... (node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"VOUTP\") ... (node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"2\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is used for assembly, the output is loaded by 24Ω instead of the intended 24kΩ, which could severely load or collapse the VOUTP-to-VOUTN output.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomaly detected. SW6 can join the positive lines of the two otherwise separate CAN buses, and R36's listed sourcing data specifies 24Ω despite its 24k schematic value."
}

